{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 126, :comments ["<b>Time</b> — All my desire is that You make me understand, and I will know Your testimonies, the opposite of my oppressors who violated Your Torah. [This is] in their old age, or in the time of their distress and their need for You. And some say: For there is a time and appointed moment for YHWH concerning those who violated Your commandments."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:48.271780075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}